 ('S01', 'Part 1', 'ill', 'sh5_1', 'Which is the tallest known mountain in the Solar System? To find it, we must leave Earth and turn our telescopes toward the red deserts of Mars. Olympus Mons is a planetary wonder that defies easy comprehension. It towers approximately twenty-one to twenty-two kilometers above the surrounding Martian plains. That is about two and a half times the height of Mount Everest above sea level, and more than twice the base-to-peak height of Mauna Kea.'),
 ('S02', 'Part 2', 'ill', 'sh5_2', 'If you placed Olympus Mons on North America, its circular base, roughly six hundred kilometers wide, would cover a region about the size of Arizona. Its summit caldera alone spans dozens of kilometers across. Like Mauna Kea, it is a shield volcano built by layer after layer of lava, only on a far larger scale. Scientists think that low gravity and a crust that stays fixed over a hotspot let it grow so tall.'),
 ('S03', 'Part 3', 'ill', 'sh5_3', 'What would it feel like to stand on the slopes of Olympus Mons? You might expect a terrifying, jagged cliff like the Himalayan peaks, but the reality is wonderfully strange. Because Olympus Mons is a huge shield volcano, its average slope is only a few degrees.'),
 ('S04', 'Part 4', 'ill', 'sh5_4', 'The mountain is so broad that you would hardly realize you were climbing; the ground would simply tilt gently upward into a dusty sky.'),
 ('S05', 'Part 5', 'ill', 'sh5_5', "Even beyond Mars, our Solar System holds other bizarre geological spires. On the asteroid Vesta, a giant impact carved a crater called Rheasilvia. NASA's Dawn spacecraft found its central peak rising roughly twenty to twenty-five kilometers above the crater floor."),
 ('S06', 'Part 6', 'ill', 'sh5_6', "On a small body with a tiny fraction of Earth's gravity, rock can stand far taller than on our dense, heavy planet."),
 ('S07', 'Part 7', 'ill', 'sh5_7', 'So which mountain is truly the highest? From sea level, Mount Everest wins. From the ocean floor, Mauna Kea wins. From the center of the Earth, Chimborazo wins. Change the ruler, and the champion changes. And beyond our world, the champions are far taller than any of them. Watch the full video to see how all three fit together.'),
